        <section>
          <h2>Accounting education. A career in technology.</h2>
          <p>I studied accounting. My career has been in software implementation and customer delivery.</p>
          <p>I earned a B.S. in Accounting and a Master of Accounting at Iowa State. That education helps me understand finance teams’ data, reporting requirements, and controls. I bring that context to software delivery for finance teams.</p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>Close to the customer and the technical work.</h2>
          <p>I started at Workiva in 2015, supporting public-company customers with SEC reporting and XBRL. At Ambra Health, I worked with customer IT teams on medical-imaging and EHR integrations. Back at Workiva as a Solutions Architect, I led implementations from requirements workshops through production use.</p>
          <p>At Citrin Cooperman, I managed a five-person implementation team and led a connected-reporting engagement through go-live and executive sign-off. Today, I’m a Senior Manager at LSL, leading Workiva delivery for city and county finance teams.</p>
          <p>The through-line is translating what a customer needs into a workable system: defining scope, working through integration and access issues, testing with users, and helping the team take ownership.</p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>Building on that experience with AI.</h2>
          <p>I develop Python tools for reporting links, formulas, and validation checks, and use AI coding tools in build and review work. My personal projects explore agent access to APIs, evidence checks, approvals, and recovery when an automated action fails.</p>
          <p>Those projects are public code and test cases, not claims of client AI deployments. They show what I’m building and give a technical team something concrete to inspect.</p>
          <p>I’m looking for forward-deployed and solutions roles that combine direct customer work with hands-on building. Finance technology is a natural fit for my domain knowledge, but the work I want to own is broader: understand the problem, work through the technical details, and help the customer put the solution to use.</p>
        </section>
